Z||000000||SloPonti||09-21-1999||05:50 PM||||have you guys seen those blue headlights from the fiero store? or some people call them hyperwhites!  does anyone have them installed on there car yet?  My brother also has a fiero and he took out his headlights and spray painted a light mist of blue on them and now at night he has the look of those hyperwhites but when you stand five feet away from his car you can see the spray paint!  it does not look good but it also doen't look bad either!  but from 15 to 100 feet away it looks really cool!!  and this does not affect the headlights at all. we can see just as good as we could before! has anyone seen these hyperwhites for the fiero any cheaper than the fiero store! they want 80.00 for them!  i can get the blue bulbs from auto zone for about 18.00 dollars a bulb but i need the lens that accepts the light- not like our fieros now where the bulb is built in! ||||reg||3
Z||000001||RICK||09-21-1999||06:59 PM||||I have them and I like them.  I'm as blind as a bat and they help me out seeing (100w high beam).  They look good also.  Instalation is easy, just follow they Hanes manual for replacing the light.  If you dont have one let me know.  As far as the price goes it is expencive but it's worth it I think.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-21-1999||09:23 PM||||I believe there is a Hela package that fits that light format.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||09-21-1999||10:42 PM||||I think JC Whitney has had the "H-4" headlights with the replaceable elements. I was going to buy a set for the 'Burb with the 80 watt low/ 120 watt high beam bulbs (I cant see at night)but just added a set of Day Lighters wired to the high beams instead.I love it when those rice burners and thier wimpy driving lights come at me- kick in the 120 watt daylighters and watch them hit the ditches!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Racer 1||09-22-1999||12:40 AM||||I have the Fiero Stores blue lights also. I think they are worse then the stock High output lights. Plus the fiero store lights make your headlight switch kind warm do to the more wattage!||||reg||13
Z||000005||Dale||09-22-1999||02:24 AM||||I have the ones from JCW H4 90/130.  I like them, but to do it right without burning up your switches you have to run a relay on them.  It's better that way because you can pull the juice straight from the battery.  I have the same ones in my truck W/4 KC's in the grill.  People dont leave their brights on with me either ( headlights and KC's on make 1040 wts). HEE HEE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
